(THE PROBLEM) Tj
0 -14 Td
(People who use sign language may face barriers when others around them do not) Tj
0 -14 Td
(understand signs. This can make everyday communication in classrooms, public) Tj
0 -14 Td
(services, and other settings more difficult. Sign languages are full languages with) Tj
0 -14 Td
(their own grammar and regional variation; they are not simply gestures or) Tj
0 -14 Td
(word-for-word versions of spoken language.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(WHY SAHAYAK) Tj
0 -14 Td
(We wanted to explore how computer vision and machine learning might help in a) Tj
0 -14 Td
(specific accessibility task. SAHAYAK uses a camera to detect hands, extracts hand) Tj
0 -14 Td
(landmarks, and predicts a label from a limited set of signs that its model has been) Tj
0 -14 Td
(trained to recognise. The website displays the prediction, and supporting speech or) Tj
0 -14 Td
(translation features may be available depending on connectivity.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(SCOPE AND HONEST LIMITATIONS) Tj
0 -14 Td
(SAHAYAK is a prototype, not a complete ISL translator. It does not understand every) Tj
0 -14 Td
(sign, sentence, facial expression, grammar rule, or regional variation. Lighting,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(camera angle, occlusion, and differences between signers can affect results. A) Tj
0 -14 Td
(broader system would need more representative data, systematic testing, and feedback) Tj
0 -14 Td
(from ISL users and experts.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
